\section*{Question 5 — Force Cost in a Tetrahedral Region}

\begin{frame}{Problem Statement and Context}

\textbf{Context:}

The following triple integral represents the force cost function in a bounded musculoskeletal system with quadratic variation along the vertical axis:

\[\iiint_E (258.70x+369.81y+z^2)\,dV\]

The solid tetrahedral region \(E\) is bounded by:
\[x=0.1,
\qquad
y=0.4,
\qquad
z=0.3,
\qquad
x+y+z=4
\]

The objective is to evaluate the \textbf{total force cost} within the system.

\vspace{0.4cm}

Shift the variables:

\[
u=x-0.1,
\qquad
v=y-0.4,
\qquad
w=z-0.3
\]

Then:

\[
u,v,w\ge0
\]

and the plane becomes:

\[
u+v+w=3.2
\]

\end{frame}

%------------------------------------------------
\subsection{Evaluating the Triple Integral}

\begin{frame}{Evaluating the Triple Integral}

Substitute:

\[
x=u+0.1,
\qquad
y=v+0.4,
\qquad
z=w+0.3
\]

into the integrand:

\[
258.70(u+0.1)+369.81(v+0.4)+(w+0.3)^2
\]

Expanding:

\[
258.70u+369.81v+w^2+0.6w+173.784
\]

The tetrahedral region becomes:

\[
u+v+w\le3.2
\]
